Subject: Carry the AOT layer over the register VM's fast-path series

What this does
  Follows the register VM's new fast paths in the generator and in the
  engine-side AOT helpers. The fused `this`-property read, the fused pair of
  argument reads, the fused postfix increment, the constant array literal,
  the null and nullish branches and the global read's per-instruction cache
  all get templates; the profiler records the new opcodes and the register
  stores the fusions introduce.

Why we need it
  The series replaced sequences the generator lowered before with single
  instructions (a `this` load plus a property read, two argument reads, a
  postfix increment, an array literal's element loads, a null test on a
  constant), so leaving them to the shared step routine would cost more
  dispatches than the old lowering did. Two helpers also stopped matching the
  handlers they mirror: `move_xfer` clears its dead source only where
  registers own their values, and `get_global` reads its per-instruction site
  cache before the cell cache.

What it adds
  qjs_aot_move_xfer()      - under deferred counting the transfer leaves the
                             source register as the handler does
  qjs_aot_get_global_site() - the site cache, then the cell probe, then the
                             global lookup; a site hit borrows the slot's value
  qjs_aot_nullish()        - null, undefined or the IsHTMLDDA object
  qjs_aot_array_const()    - a fresh array from a constant-pool template
  templates                - get_this_field, get_this_field2, get_arg2,
                             post_inc, post_dec, branch_null, branch_not_null,
                             branch_nullish, branch_not_nullish, array_const
  profile hooks            - the four null branches count as conditional
                             branches; get_arg2's first store and the fused
                             `this` read's receiver record register facts

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

Notes
  A bound unit on box2d still matches 307/308 profile records (100.0% of
  profiled ops), the digest test is 3/3 and box2d's checksum is unchanged in
  every mode. After the hooks the profile's register facts and branch totals
  are equal to the pre-series values; the per-pc facts fall by 142 lines
  because the profiled functions are 162 instructions shorter after the
  fusions, not because a hook was lost.

